{%- comment -%}
  Bamboo Bicycle Club — Collection / listing (2026 redesign).
  Renders {{ collection }} products in the .bbc-rd stamp-card style with a
  funding cause line, sort, and pagination. Styling lives in
  assets/bbc-redesign-2026.css. Guarded so it degrades off a collection page.
{%- endcomment -%}


<div class="bbc-rd bbc-rd-collection{% if collection.handle == 'home-build-kits' %} kvh-page{% endif %}">

  {%- comment -%} ============================================================
    HOME-BUILD-KITS HERO (2026-08-24, James: "for the build a bike create a hero
    with some home build kits quick links and link to Julian home build kit video
    ... and create an introduction to building a bike at home").
    Family format (forest / gutter axis / culm / film right), gated to THIS
    collection only - every other collection keeps the paper head below.
    THE FILM (v2 2026-08-24, James: "video quality is very poor, use So1spIs9_jM"):
    44s from the COMPLETE 1080p master of "Carbon Lugs for Bamboo Bike Frames
    Explained" - plans on the bench, a lug wrapped by hand, the finished bamboo
    road bike, riding through the city. 1160x1000, 6.2MB. v1 mixed a 1080p flatlay
    with a 360p home build upscaled 1.4x - the upscale was the visible softness.
    QUICK LINKS: chips generated from the collection's own products, so a new
    kit appears in the rail automatically and a retired one leaves it.
    JULIAN: links OUT to Julian Goulding's own YouTube film "I built my own
    Bamboo Bike Frame!" [ckCwJXJGKD0]. Third-party video - the rights register
    covers offline classroom use with credit, NOT re-hosting, so the site links
    to his upload rather than serving a copy. That is also the more convincing
    social proof: a real customer on his own channel.
    .kvh-* is a fresh namespace (same reasoning as the why-bamboo .dvh-*): the
    cascade war cannot reach names no other sheet mentions. --bbc-gutter comes
    from bbc-align via .bbc-rd. Playback = the estate's hardened pattern.
  ============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if collection.handle == 'home-build-kits' -%}
  <header class="kvh">
    <div class="kvh-copy">
      <nav class="rd-crumb kvh-crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a><span class="rd-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">{{ collection.title | escape }}</span></nav>
      <p class="kvh-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | default: 'Build at home' }}</p>
      <h1 class="kvh-h1">{{ section.settings.kits_title | default: 'a bike you build yourself.' }}</h1>
      <p class="kvh-lede">{{ section.settings.kits_intro | default: 'Everything arrives in one box: graded bamboo, the lugs, the jig and every tool. No welding and no workshop - most builders start with zero experience, and the manual and video course carry you the whole way.' }}</p>
      <div class="kvh-chips" role="list" aria-label="Choose your kit">
        {%- for product in collection.products limit: 8 -%}
          <a class="kvh-chip" role="listitem" href="{{ product.url }}"><span class="kvh-chip-t">{{ product.title | replace: ' Frame Build Kit', '' | replace: ' Home Build Kit', '' | replace: ' Build Kit', '' | replace: ' Frame Kit', '' | replace: ' Kit with Resins', ' Flax' | replace: ' Kit', '' }}</span></a>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
      {%- if section.settings.julian_url != blank -%}
        <p class="kvh-watch"><a class="kvh-watch-a" href="{{ section.settings.julian_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span class="kvh-watch-t">{{ section.settings.julian_label | default: "Watch Julian build his: 'I built my own Bamboo Bike Frame' &rarr;" }}</span></a></p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    <div class="kvh-media">
      <img class="kvh-img" src="{{ 'bbc-rd-wb-kit.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="A bamboo frame kit laid out: graded tubes, lugs, jig parts and the build manual" width="1200" height="900" fetchpriority="high">
      {%- if section.settings.kits_video_url != blank -%}
        <video class="kvh-film" muted loop playsinline webkit-playsinline preload="metadata"
               {% if section.settings.kits_video_poster != blank %}poster="{{ section.settings.kits_video_poster }}"{% endif %}
               aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" src="{{ section.settings.kits_video_url }}"></video>
      {%- endif -%}
      <div class="kvh-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
  </header>
  {%- comment -%} BUILDER ANSWERS (2026-08-24, from the vault email-mining data):
    shipping is the single biggest kit question (~1,170 asks, heavily international),
    build time is second (~240, "can it be done in a weekend?"), and 72% of kit
    builders need a fork - previously buried. Three answers, right under the hero,
    before anyone has to ask. All three lines are estate-verified claims. {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kvh-answers" role="list">
    <div class="kvh-answer" role="listitem"><b>{{ section.settings.ans1_head | default: 'Ships worldwide' }}</b><span>{{ section.settings.ans1_body | default: 'Tracked delivery to 45 countries.' }}</span></div>
    <div class="kvh-answer" role="listitem"><b>{{ section.settings.ans2_head | default: 'Built in a weekend' }}</b><span>{{ section.settings.ans2_body | default: 'Hand tools and the video course - no workshop needed.' }}</span></div>
    <div class="kvh-answer" role="listitem"><b>{{ section.settings.ans3_head | default: 'Need a fork or parts?' }}</b><span>{{ section.settings.ans3_body | default: 'Most builders add one.' }} <a class="kvh-ans-a" href="{{ section.settings.ans3_url | default: '/collections/component-packs' }}"><span class="kvh-ans-t">{{ section.settings.ans3_link | default: 'Component packs &rarr;' }}</span></a></span></div>
  </div>
  {%- else -%}
  <section class="rd-pad-sm rd-paper">
    <div class="rd-wrap rd-coll-head">
      <span class="rd-eyebrow">{%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}{% if collection.handle == 'home-build-kits' or collection.handle == 'road' or collection.handle == 'gravel-adventure' or collection.handle == 'mtb' or collection.handle == 'balance-bikes' %}{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}{% else %}Everything we make{% endif %}{%- elsif collection.handle == 'gift' -%}Give a build{%- elsif collection.handle == 'maker-shop' -%}From our workshop{%- else -%}Build at home{%- endif -%}</span>
      {%- if collection -%}
{%- comment -%} LAW 9 (CONSISTENCY-SPEC 2026-08-07): breadcrumb {%- endcomment -%}
<nav class="rd-crumb rd-crumb--onlight" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a><span class="rd-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">{{ collection.title | escape }}</span></nav>
        <h1>{{ collection.title }}</h1>
        {%- if collection.description != blank -%}
          <div class="rd-lede rd-mt2 rd-mw-62ch">{{ collection.description }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
{%- comment -%} LAW 9 (CONSISTENCY-SPEC 2026-08-07): breadcrumb {%- endcomment -%}
<nav class="rd-crumb rd-crumb--onlight" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a><span class="rd-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">{{ collection.title | escape }}</span></nav>
        <h1>{{ section.settings.fallback_title | default: 'frame kits' }}</h1>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endif -%}

  <section class="rd-pad">
    <div class="rd-wrap">

      {%- if section.settings.cause_line != blank -%}
        <div class="rd-cause-bar">{%- if collection.handle == 'gift' -%}Every gift you give helps fund accredited skills courses inside prisons and schools.{%- elsif collection.handle == 'maker-shop' or collection.handle == 'component-packs' -%}Every order helps fund accredited skills courses inside prisons and schools.{%- else -%}{{ section.settings.cause_line }}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign kit_handles = "home-build-kits,road,gravel-adventure,mtb,balance-bikes,component-packs" | split: "," -%}
      {%- if kit_handles contains collection.handle and section.settings.proof_line != blank -%}
        <div class="rd-cause-bar rd-proof-bar">{{ section.settings.proof_line }} <a href="/pages/why-bamboo">See the testing &rarr;</a></div>
      {%- endif -%}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if collection -%}
        {%- paginate collection.products by section.settings.per_page -%}
          <div class="rd-coll-bar">
            <span class="rd-coll-count">{{ collection.products_count }} {% if collection.handle == 'home-build-kits' %}{% if collection.products_count == 1 %}kit{% else %}kits{% endif %}{% elsif collection.handle == 'component-packs' %}{% if collection.products_count == 1 %}pack{% else %}packs{% endif %}{% else %}{% if collection.products_count == 1 %}product{% else %}products{% endif %}{% endif %}</span>
            {%- if collection.sort_options.size > 0 -%}
              <form method="get" class="rd-sort">
                <label for="rd-sortby">Sort</label>
                <select id="rd-sortby" name="sort_by" onchange="this.form.submit()">
                  {%- assign cur = collection.sort_by | default: collection.default_sort_by -%}
                  {%- for opt in collection.sort_options -%}
                    <option value="{{ opt.value }}"{% if opt.value == cur %} selected{% endif %}>{{ opt.name }}</option>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
              </form>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>

          <div class="rd-grid rd-g3">
            {%- for product in collection.products -%}
              <a class="rd-reveal rd-card rd-stamp" href="{{ product.url }}">
                <div class="rd-ph">
                  {%- if product.featured_image -%}
                    {%- comment -%}
                      Product cards had NO srcset — a single hardcoded 800px served to a 359px
                      slot at every DPR, on every card, on every collection page. Measured
                      2026-07-29 at both DPR1 and DPR2: served 800, CSS 359, srcset absent.
                      Shopify's responsive-image pattern is image_url with width candidates plus
                      sizes; the grid is 3-up above 990px, 2-up on tablet, 1-up on mobile, which
                      is what the sizes expression below describes. Tuned to 28vw after measuring: 33vw
                      overstates the real 359px slot at 1280, which made DPR2 jump to the 1200w
                      candidate. 28vw resolves to ~358 CSS px, so DPR2 lands on 800w.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 800 }}"
                         srcset="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 200 }} 200w,
                                 {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w,
                                 {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w,
                                 {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w,
                                 {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w"
                         sizes="(min-width: 990px) 28vw, (min-width: 750px) 45vw, 92vw"
                         alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | escape | default: product.title }}"
                         width="{{ product.featured_image.width }}" height="{{ product.featured_image.height }}" loading="lazy">
                    {%- if product.images[1] -%}
                      <img class="rd-ph-alt" src="{{ product.images[1] | image_url: width: 800 }}"
                           srcset="{{ product.images[1] | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w, {{ product.images[1] | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w, {{ product.images[1] | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w"
                           sizes="(min-width: 990px) 28vw, (min-width: 750px) 45vw, 92vw"
                           alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="{{ product.images[1].width }}" height="{{ product.images[1].height }}" loading="lazy">
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- else -%}
                    <img src="{{ 'bbc-rd-prod-gravel.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="{{ product.title | escape }}" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy">
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- if product.type != blank -%}<span class="rd-tag rd-lime rd-cardtag">{{ product.type }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                </div>
                <div class="rd-body">
                  <h2 class="rd-reveal rd-fs-18px">{{ product.title }}</h2>
                  <div class="rd-price">{% if product.price == 0 %}Free — postage only{% elsif product.price_varies %}From {{ product.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}{% else %}{{ product.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}{% endif %}{% if product.compare_at_price > product.price %}<span class="rd-was">{{ product.compare_at_price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>{% endif %}</div>
                </div>
              </a>
            {%- else -%}
              <p class="rd-lede">No products in this collection yet.</p>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>

          {%- if paginate.pages > 1 -%}
            <nav class="rd-pagination" aria-label="Pagination">
              {%- for part in paginate.parts -%}
                {%- if part.is_link -%}
                  <a href="{{ part.url }}" aria-label="Page {{ part.title }}">{{ part.title }}</a>
                {%- else -%}
                  <span{% if part.title == paginate.current_page %} class="rd-cur" aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ part.title }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </nav>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endpaginate -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <p class="rd-lede">Add this section to a collection template to list its products.</p>
      {%- endif -%}

    </div>
  </section>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
/* .kvh-* home-build-kits hero - fresh namespace, see the head comment. */
.kvh{display:grid;grid-template-columns:0.82fr 1fr;align-items:stretch;min-height:clamp(540px,78vh,880px);min-height:clamp(540px,78svh,880px);background:var(--forest,#003C32);overflow:hidden;isolation:isolate}
.kvh-copy{position:relative;z-index:3;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;padding:clamp(26px,4.8vh,80px) clamp(20px,2.6vw,48px) clamp(30px,5.4vh,84px) var(--bbc-gutter,clamp(32px,6vw,120px));container-type:inline-size}
.kvh-copy::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:calc(var(--bbc-gutter,48px) - 34px);top:13%;bottom:13%;width:3px;border-radius:3px;background:repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom,var(--lime,#D4FD62) 0 20px,rgba(6,35,28,.55) 20px 24px)}
.kvh-crumb{margin-bottom:clamp(12px,2vh,22px)}
.kvh-crumb,.kvh-crumb a{color:rgba(230,220,200,.72)!important;text-shadow:none}
.kvh-crumb a:hover{color:var(--lime,#D4FD62)!important}
.kvh-crumb [aria-current]{color:var(--lime,#D4FD62)}
.kvh-eyebrow{margin:0 0 clamp(10px,1.8vh,20px);font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--lime,#D4FD62)}
.kvh .kvh-h1{margin:0;color:var(--bone,#E6DCC8)!important;font-size:clamp(2.2rem,6.6vw,5rem);line-height:1.02;letter-spacing:-.01em;text-wrap:balance}
.kvh-lede{margin:clamp(14px,2.2vh,24px) 0 0;max-width:48ch;color:rgba(238,243,236,.92);font-size:clamp(1rem,1.9cqw,1.2rem);line-height:1.55}
/* THE UNIQUE DEVICE: the kit rail. One chip per kit, straight from the collection,
   so the hero doubles as navigation - the "quick links" of the brief. Lime outline
   chips (the estate tag language); hover fills. */
.kvh-chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:9px;margin-top:clamp(18px,2.8vh,28px)}
/* COLOUR ARMOUR v2 (2026-08-24, James: "buttons and text is black on a dark
   background" - correct: chips measured rgb(14,26,23), watch link rgb(20,33,28)).
   A cross-origin estate rule paints these ANCHORS dark with !important and even a
   (0,6,1)+!important override did not take on the deployed page. Ended the war by
   moving the text into SPANS: anchor colour rules do not target spans, and a
   DIRECT rule on the span - any specificity - always beats a colour the span
   would merely inherit from its <a>. The anchor can be painted whatever the
   estate likes; the visible glyphs are the span's. */
.kvh-chip{display:inline-block;padding:7px 14px;border:1.5px solid rgba(212,253,98,.55);border-radius:999px;font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.02em;text-decoration:none!important;transition:background .15s ease}
.kvh-chip .kvh-chip-t{color:var(--lime,#D4FD62)}
.kvh-chip:hover,.kvh-chip:focus-visible{background:var(--lime,#D4FD62)}
.kvh-chip:hover .kvh-chip-t,.kvh-chip:focus-visible .kvh-chip-t{color:var(--forest,#003C32)}
.kvh-watch{margin:clamp(14px,2.2vh,22px) 0 0;font-size:14px}
.kvh-watch-a{font-weight:700;text-decoration:underline!important;text-underline-offset:4px;text-decoration-color:rgba(238,243,236,.6)!important}
.kvh-watch-a .kvh-watch-t{color:rgba(238,243,236,.88)}
.kvh-watch-a:hover .kvh-watch-t{color:var(--lime,#D4FD62)}
.kvh-media{position:relative;z-index:1;min-height:0;overflow:hidden}
.kvh-img,.kvh-film{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block}
.kvh-film{opacity:0;transition:opacity .6s ease;z-index:1}
.kvh-film.is-on{opacity:1}
.kvh-scrim{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:2;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--forest,#003C32) 0%,rgba(0,60,50,.34) 28%,rgba(0,60,50,0) 64%);pointer-events:none}
@media(max-width:1199px){
  .kvh{grid-template-columns:1fr;min-height:0}
  .kvh-media{grid-row:1;height:clamp(240px,38svh,440px)}
  .kvh-copy{grid-row:2;padding-block:clamp(28px,5vw,56px)}
  .kvh-copy::before{position:relative;inset:auto;width:68px;height:3px;margin:0 0 18px;background:repeating-linear-gradient(to right,var(--lime,#D4FD62) 0 20px,rgba(6,35,28,.55) 20px 24px)}
  .kvh-scrim{background:linear-gradient(0deg,var(--forest,#003C32) 0%,rgba(0,60,50,.32) 26%,rgba(0,60,50,0) 62%)}
}
@media(max-width:749px){
  .kvh-media{height:clamp(180px,26svh,320px)}
  /* the rail IS the action on this page, so it stays right after the headline;
     the intro drops below it. Film trimmed so headline + rail land on screen. */
  .kvh-copy{display:flex}
  .kvh-crumb{order:1}
  .kvh-eyebrow{order:2}
  .kvh .kvh-h1{order:3}
  .kvh-chips{order:4;margin-top:clamp(14px,2.2vh,22px)}
  .kvh-lede{order:5;margin-top:clamp(14px,2.2vh,22px)}
  .kvh-watch{order:6}
}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){ .kvh-film{display:none} }
/* Builder answers - the three researched questions, as a quiet forest strip
   bridging hero to grid. */
.kvh-answers{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:0;background:var(--forest,#003C32);border-top:1px solid rgba(212,253,98,.25)}
.kvh-answer{padding:18px var(--bbc-gutter,32px) 20px;border-right:1px solid rgba(230,220,200,.14)}
.kvh-answer:last-child{border-right:0}
.kvh-answer b{display:block;color:var(--lime,#D4FD62);font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:4px}
.kvh-answer span{color:rgba(238,243,236,.85);font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.45}
.kvh-ans-a{font-weight:700;text-decoration:underline!important;text-underline-offset:3px;text-decoration-color:rgba(212,253,98,.7)!important}
.kvh-ans-a .kvh-ans-t{color:var(--lime,#D4FD62)}
@media(max-width:899px){.kvh-answers{grid-template-columns:1fr}.kvh-answer{border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(230,220,200,.14);padding:14px var(--bbc-gutter,18px)}.kvh-answer:last-child{border-bottom:0}}
/* CSS fixes below the hero (James: "css is very poor"), scoped to this section:
   1. The proof line rendered JAMMED into the cause line ("...schools.Independently
      strength-tested...") because .rd-proof-bar is nested INSIDE .rd-cause-bar with
      no separation. Breathing room + its own top rule.
   2. Card hierarchy was flat - title and price both 18px. Price is the deciding
      number on a listing; it leads now.
   3. Product photo gets a quiet zoom on hover so the cards read as clickable. */
.bbc-rd-collection .rd-cause-bar .rd-proof-bar{margin-top:10px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,60,50,.18)}
.bbc-rd-collection .rd-grid .rd-card .rd-body h2{font-size:16px!important;line-height:1.3}
.bbc-rd-collection .rd-grid .rd-card .rd-price{font-size:21px;font-weight:800;margin-top:6px}
.bbc-rd-collection .rd-grid .rd-card .rd-ph{overflow:hidden}
.bbc-rd-collection .rd-grid .rd-card .rd-ph img{transition:transform .35s ease}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){.bbc-rd-collection .rd-grid .rd-card:hover .rd-ph img{transform:scale(1.04)}}
/* v3 (2026-08-24, James ran the page: "css is still poor" - he was right, and the
   faults only showed in a SCREENSHOT, not in measurements):
   4. The cause/proof bar rendered as a ~180px dark SLAB, centred, dominating the
      page before a single product. On the kits page it becomes a slim left-ruled
      note: transparent, lime rule, left-aligned, one visual voice.
   5. The answers strip wrapped raggedly and orphaned the arrow ("Component packs /
      ->"). Nowrap on the links, tighter leading, balanced padding.
   6. Every card wore the SAME "FRAME BUILD KIT" tag - a label that distinguishes
      nothing is noise; hidden on this page only (other collections mix types and
      keep it).
   7. Rhythm: the grid section opened with ~90px of dead bone above the slab;
      tightened so strip -> note -> grid reads as one page. */
.kvh-page .rd-cause-bar{background:transparent!important;color:var(--forest,#003C32)!important;border:0!important;border-left:3px solid var(--lime,#D4FD62)!important;border-radius:0!important;padding:10px 18px!important;text-align:left!important;max-width:none!important;margin:0 0 26px!important;font-size:14.5px!important;box-shadow:none!important}
.kvh-page .rd-cause-bar a{color:var(--forest,#003C32)!important}
.kvh-page .rd-cause-bar .rd-proof-bar{background:transparent!important;border:0!important;border-top:0!important;padding:4px 0 0!important;margin-top:4px!important;font-size:13px!important;opacity:.78;text-align:left!important}
.kvh-page section.rd-pad{padding-top:clamp(30px,4vh,44px)!important}
.kvh-page .rd-cardtag{display:none!important}
.kvh-answer{padding:16px var(--bbc-gutter,32px) 18px}
.kvh-answer span{display:block;max-width:34ch}
.kvh-answer a.kvh-ans-a{white-space:nowrap}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% javascript %}
/* Kits hero film - the estate's hardened pattern (start on canplay, reveal on
   playing; gates leave the flatlay photo). */
(function () {
  var v = document.querySelector('.kvh-film');
  if (!v) return;
  if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;
  /* phone gate removed 2026-08-24 - James: hero films must play on mobile too */
  var conn = navigator.connection || navigator.mozConnection || navigator.webkitConnection;
  if (conn && (conn.saveData || /(^|-)2g$/.test(conn.effectiveType || ''))) return;
  v.muted = true; v.defaultMuted = true;
  function start() { var p = v.play(); if (p && p.catch) p.catch(function () {}); }
  v.addEventListener('playing', function () { v.classList.add('is-on'); }, { once: true });
  v.setAttribute('preload', 'auto');
  v.load();
  if (v.readyState >= 3) start();
  else v.addEventListener('canplay', start, { once: true });
  document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function () {
    if (document.hidden) { v.pause(); }
    else if (v.classList.contains('is-on')) { start(); }
  });
})();
{% endjavascript %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collection 2026 (new)",
  "tag": "div",
  "class": "bbc-rd-collection-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "Build at home"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "fallback_title",
